# Copy to ~/.config/tmux-rc/tunnel.env — read by tmux-rc-tunnel.service, which stays
# inactive until this file exists. Contents depend entirely on which tunnel client you
# run (see that unit's ExecStart); this repo doesn't ship one.
#
# Keep credentials HERE rather than in the unit or on the command line: the unit is
# committed to git, and flags are visible in `ps`. Prefer an auth mode that refreshes
# itself — anything needing a periodic browser login will strand an unattended host.
#
# Example shape for a client that takes a subdomain and a local port:
#TUNNEL_SLUG=your-host
#TUNNEL_PORT=18030
#TUNNEL_OWNER=you@example.com
